# A-to-Z Development Plan: IoT-Based Smart Voting and Public Bill Archive System

This plan is structured for a realistic prototype build, beginning with a working local system and then expanding toward a final demonstration. The goal is to build and validate each subsystem independently before integrating everything into one end-to-end system.

The most important rule: do not build the entire system at once. Build, test, and stabilize each module separately before connecting them.

---

## 1. Project vision

This project combines:

- an administrative website for managing members, terms, bills, and sessions
- a backend API for validating votes and publishing results
- an ESP32 voting terminal with fingerprint verification
- a public bill archive where finalized results and proposal PDFs are displayed

### Core system flow

Admin Website
  -> Backend API
  -> SQLite Database
  -> Session / Bill / Vote management

ESP32 Terminal
  -> Wi-Fi
  -> Backend API
  -> Fingerprint verification
  -> Vote submission

Public Website
  -> Backend API
  -> Finalized records only
  -> PDF and result archive

