## 6. Database design

The backend database should contain these main records:

| Table | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| users | hosts, members, roles, and account status |
| parliamentary_terms | parliamentary terms and their current status |
| term_memberships | which members belong to which term |
| fingerprint_references | AS608 template IDs linked to members |
| bills | bill title, question, languages, metadata |
| documents | proposal PDF path, size, checksum |
| sessions | session status, times, options, and approval state |
| votes | latest accepted vote per member per session |
| vote_audit | accepted revisions and vote events |
| audit_events | admin actions, approvals, and system events |

Important rules:
- store only fingerprint template references, never raw biometric data
- enforce a unique record for each member/session vote
- record vote revisions in an audit table if revision is allowed
- keep PDFs outside the database and store metadata only in the DB
- let the server decide the final vote acceptance and deadline logic

