## 8. Session state machine

The system should use a clear and controlled voting lifecycle.

Draft
  -> Assistant Host prepares the bill and document

Pending Approval
  -> waiting for Main Host review

Approved
  -> authorized to begin

Active
  -> accepts valid votes until deadline or closure

Finalized
  -> votes are locked and the result is published

Rejected
  -> proposal is rejected and remains non-public

Critical rules:
- sessions should not be switched on/off manually without proper server logic
- when a session expires, the backend must stop accepting new votes and finalize the result
- a device showing an old active screen must never override the server-authorized session state
- the public archive should show only finalized results, not individual member choices

